    "controller_support": "full",
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Space is Red</strong> is an alt-history sci-fi horror visual novel.\u00a0\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game takes place aboard a Soviet starship in an alternate future where the USSR still exists and competes with the US for dominance in space. After a hyperspace jump to evade an ambush, the crew finds itself near a mysterious planet in a poorly explored sector of the known galaxy. Strange occurrences begin, and suspicion grows among the crew that a traitor may be in their midst.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3357480/extras/55845d011530e76dbfefab3d2de0fb13.avif?t=1736935892\" data-has-big width=800 height=448 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The visuals are styled like a black-and-white comic book, drawing inspiration from retro-horror manga. Expect multiple endings, detective elements, numerous deaths, and, of course, an alien presence.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Space is Red</strong> is a radical reimagining of the first Russian full-length visual novel, <i>\u00ab\u041a\u0440\u0430\u0441\u043d\u044b\u0439 \u043a\u043e\u0441\u043c\u043e\u0441\u00bb</i> (<i>Red Space</i>), originally released in 2007. This game was never translated into English and has never been available digitally.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Space is Red</strong> is an alt-history sci-fi horror visual novel.\u00a0\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game takes place aboard a Soviet starship in an alternate future where the USSR still exists and competes with the US for dominance in space. After a hyperspace jump to evade an ambush, the crew finds itself near a mysterious planet in a poorly explored sector of the known galaxy. Strange occurrences begin, and suspicion grows among the crew that a traitor may be in their midst.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3357480/extras/55845d011530e76dbfefab3d2de0fb13.avif?t=1736935892\" data-has-big width=800 height=448 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The visuals are styled like a black-and-white comic book, drawing inspiration from retro-horror manga. Expect multiple endings, detective elements, numerous deaths, and, of course, an alien presence.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Space is Red</strong> is a radical reimagining of the first Russian full-length visual novel, <i>\u00ab\u041a\u0440\u0430\u0441\u043d\u044b\u0439 \u043a\u043e\u0441\u043c\u043e\u0441\u00bb</i> (<i>Red Space</i>), originally released in 2007. This game was never translated into English and has never been available digitally.</p>",
    "short_description": "Space is Red is an alt-history sci-fi horror visual novel set aboard a Soviet starship in an alternate future. The game features multiple endings, detective elements, mysterious deaths, and, of course, an alien presence.",
